{"type":"Feature","properties":{"kind":"port_limits","cargo":[],"osm":["way/198032208","way/208805042","relation/17726211","way/198032201","way/198032203","relation/9369410","way/198032205","relation/7027966","way/1198736067"],"source":"Derived: the convex hull of this port's terminals from OpenStreetMap, grown by 200 m, then cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it (the sea within its coastline, rivers, docks and basins), with the terminals kept whole","licence":"ODbL-1.0","reviewed_at":"2026-11-23","clip":"water","disjoint":"The 2nd Container Port is mapped as two areas: the terminal on the harbour, and a yard about 230 m back from the water, 15 m from the terminal, beside the 新生滯洪池 flood detention pond. Nothing OpenStreetMap maps joins the yard to the harbour, so it stands as a part of its own.","note":"OpenStreetMap maps no port limits for Kaohsiung. These are the hull of the 1st to 7th container centres, grown by 200 m and cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it, with the centres kept whole: the harbour channel from the 1st centre down to the second harbour entrance, and the basins between the centres. Cijin and the Qianzhen waterfront are land and left out. A scan of OpenStreetMap finds no homes, schools, hospitals or places of worship inside. It finds two place names on the 6th centre for Hongmaogang (紅毛港), the village cleared to build it, a Tudigong label on the 4th centre, and at the edge 300 m² of an outdoor exhibition area by the 6th centre tagged as housing."},"geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[120.30916,22.557918],[120.308936,22.558087],[120.308674,22.557895],[120.308031,22.558055],[120.307328,22.557554],[120.307263,22.557336],[120.30489,22.55985],[120.303884,22.561148],[120.303566,22.564372],[120.303141,22.565236],[120.3026,22.565673],[120.302471,22.566013],[120.30171,22.567],[120.30059,22.56801],[120.29987,22.56915],[120.29902,22.56977],[120.29774,22.57156],[120.29576,22.57384],[120.295252,22.574652],[120.292192,22.578469],